cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite the manuscript it supports (once published) and, if you reuse a specific version of this repository, its archived Zenodo release."
title: "Data Availability — Reading Natural Fractures from Conventional Well Logs: A Critical Review of Machine-Learning Validation and Generalization"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Simao"
    affiliation: "Universiti Teknologi PETRONAS"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/REPLACE-WITH-USERNAME/REPLACE-WITH-REPO-NAME"
abstract: >
  Full literature-screening and extraction dataset supporting a critical
  literature review of machine-learning approaches to inferring natural
  fractures from conventional wireline logs. Documents 96 screened
  candidate papers, 53 papers taken to full-text extraction, and the
  42-paper (43-entry) final review corpus, each with a 26-field
  extraction record, validation-level and evidence-strength
  classification, and resolved Author-Year citation with DOI.
keywords:
  - natural fractures
  - well logs
  - machine learning
  - literature review
  - systematic review
  - petrophysics
  - fracture porosity
  - validation
